      "rain": {
        "$type": "color",
        "$value": "rgba( 0, 187, 0, .55 )",
        "$extensions": {
          "csc": {
            "comment": "the matrix rain on the home page and section landings (assets/js/custom.js, §17 in custom.css). A texture, not a feature: the alpha is the only thing standing between \"faint CRT\" and \"unreadable page\", so keep it low. Green, not blue — the rain is the one place the identity colour is allowed to run the whole viewport.",
            "variants": {
              "hacker-light": {
                "$value": "rgba( 11, 95, 196, .10 )",
                "comment": "the matrix rain on the home page and section landings (assets/js/custom.js, §17 in custom.css). Near-invisible in daylight on purpose: falling glyphs over white are noise the dark variant can carry and paper cannot. This is the token doing that job — the JS is the same code in every variant."
              },
              "cyber": {
                "$value": "rgba( 0, 255, 65, .70 )",
                "comment": "the matrix rain on the home page and section landings (assets/js/custom.js, §17 in custom.css). A texture, not a feature: the alpha is the only thing standing between \"faint CRT\" and \"unreadable page\", so keep it low."
              }
